\begin_layout Standard
The first frequency moves by 0.15 per cent from the coarse to the medium mesh and by 0.04 per cent from the medium to the fine one; the medium mesh, under four seconds per run, is the default. The refinement is not uniform in the three directions, so the observed order of convergence is only indicative. What remains, +0.3 to +0.4 per cent above the exact beam value, is not a mesh error: it is the plate effect. A tongue several times wider than thick bends a little like a plate, with the stiffness 
\begin_inset Formula $D=Eh^{3}/\left(12(1-\nu^{2})\right)$
\end_inset
 instead of 
\begin_inset Formula $Eh^{3}/12$
\end_inset
 per unit width in the limit of cylindrical bending, which would raise the frequency by 
\begin_inset Formula $1/\sqrt{1-\nu^{2}}-1\approx4.5$
\end_inset
