\begin_layout Section
Measuring the whole instrument
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The simplest global test uses the bellows itself. Hang a known weight on the bellows, close the air valve, press no button, and let the weight pull the bellows open; read the pressure with a U-tube on the air valve, and film the bellows with a ruler next to it. The leak is the volume displaced by the bellows divided by the time of the full drop. For a bellows that moves about 10 litres, Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:chute"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset
 gives the equivalent hole at 500 Pa. The longer the drop, the tighter the instrument.
\end_layout

